<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-reggae-skank" category="Clean" order="230" instrument="guitar" style="Reggae">
  <description>Thin, bright, short off-beat skank: a solid-state 2x12 with treble up and the bass cut hard so the chop never fights the bass and organ, light compression and a short splash of studio spring on the attack. Bridge pickup, top three or four strings, choke every chord short.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Reggae</tag><tag>Bright</tag><tag>Spring Reverb</tag><tag>Compressed</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/lessons/bob-marley-reggae-rhythm-guitar" title="Guitar World: Bob Marley's essential reggae rhythm styles"/>
    <source url="https://www.tdpri.com/threads/reggae-sound-on-amp-setting.1016082/" title="TDPRI: reggae sound amp settings (Tuff Lion's 7-5-4)"/>
    <source url="http://www.how-to-play-reggae.com/How-to-Get-The-Reggae-Guitar-Sound.html" title="How to Play Reggae: how to get the reggae guitar sound"/>
    <source url="https://bassculture.substack.com/p/the-deep-roots-of-reverb-in-reggae" title="Bass Culture: the deep roots of reverb in reggae and dub"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
